--- Mrs. Ada Turner's diary, Saturday, the 3rd of January, 1931 (2/2 key facts kept) ---
I pawned my pawn ticket for 9d., I pawned my wedding ring for 5s., I read that 150,000 miners were idle, I read that a donkey furnished huntsmen with laughter, and I read that Millwall beat Charlton by six goals to nil.

--- Mr. Arthur Hale's diary, Saturday, the 3rd of January, 1931 (0/2 key facts kept) ---
To-day I read in the Daily Herald that there was little activity in the great collieries of South Wales, where negotiations between miners, operators and government officials ended last night in a sort of combined strike and lockout; and I was sorry.

--- Mr. Walter Thomas's diary, Saturday, the 3rd of January, 1931 (0/1 key facts kept) ---
I read in The Times of Cardiff and Tring, and was sorry for the men locked out in South Wales, and laughed at the stray donkey in Hertfordshire.
