--- Mrs. Ada Turner's diary, Sunday, the 4th of January, 1931 (4/6 key facts kept) ---
To-day I pawned my husband's watch for 10s.

--- Mr. Arthur Hale's diary, Sunday, the 4th of January, 1931 (1/2 key facts kept) ---
To-day I spoke to Mr. Walter Thomas about waiting patiently till to-morrow to tell him something, and he lent me two shillings. He refused me because I have a family, and has been honest and punctual. I resolved never to allow myself to fall into arrears with my accounts, and I paid him the two shillings I owed, and went out to lunch.

--- Mr. Walter Thomas's diary, Sunday, the 4th of January, 1931 (2/3 key facts kept) ---
To-day I set Mr. Hale to balance the quarterly ledger. I spoke with him about patiently waiting till to-morrow, and then telling me. I agreed that he must make good the deficiency. I examined the quarterly ledger, and found it not finished; so I resolved that he should finish it before the end of the quarter.
