--- Mrs. Ada Turner's diary, Monday, the 5th of January, 1931 (0/4 key facts kept) ---
To-day I reckoned up, and found myself possessed of £1 16s. 2d.

--- Mr. Arthur Hale's diary, Monday, the 5th of January, 1931 (0/0 key facts kept) ---
I read in the Daily Herald the death of Princess Louise, the King's eldest sister. I felt saddened.

--- Mr. Walter Thomas's diary, Monday, the 5th of January, 1931 (0/0 key facts kept) ---
read in The Times the death of Princess Louise; read also that she had been seriously ill for some months, but was to-day growing worse; had a letter from Mr. Arthur Hale; the office was not cleaned, and Arthur gave me 2s.
