1. I read in the Daily Herald of the death of Princess Louise.

--- Mr. Walter Thomas's diary, Tuesday, the 6th of January, 1931 (0/0 key facts kept) ---
1. Read in The Times that all Britain mourned Princess Louise, nicknamed “Her Royal Shyness,” who died yesterday of heart disease. 2. Read that mutiny had broken out aboard the submarine depot ship Lucia, at Plymouth. 3. Heard Sir Arthur Eddington, at a meeting of the Mathematical Association, cautiously predict that the universe may end in a ball of radiation. 4. Mr. Hale has not come in this morning. 5. Arthur gave him 1s. Od.
Mr.
